# atmos_factorio_mods

Monorepo for Factorio mod development (target: Factorio **2.1**).

## Language

- Default language for code, comments, commits and `info.json` is **English**.
- Docs are written per language in separate source files; the combined files are **generated**:
  - Sources: `README_EN.md` + `README_RU.md`, `changelog_EN.txt` + `changelog_RU.txt`.
  - Outputs: `README.md` (EN part, `---`, RU part) and `changelog.txt` (per version and category: EN entries, then RU entries; RU categories match EN by name or by position).
  - Never edit `README.md` / `changelog.txt` by hand; edit the `_EN` / `_RU` sources and run `py -3 scripts/build_docs.py [mod]` (`--check` verifies they are up to date). `pack_mod.py` rebuilds them automatically.
  - `_RU` changelog must have the same versions and category order as `_EN`.
- Keep EN and `_RU` sources in sync when behavior or version notes change.
- Chat with the user may be in Russian; authored project files stay EN unless `_RU`.

## Locales

- Primary in-game locales: `locale/en/` and `locale/ru/`.
- Mirror keys across both; do not leave RU keys missing for player-facing strings.
- Prefer locale keys over hard-coded `localised_*` English strings when text is shown to players.

## Layout

- One mod per top-level folder (e.g. `atmos_shotgun_tiers/`).
- Folder name may differ from portal `info.json` `name`; never rename `name` if it would break saves or the portal page.
- Packaging scripts live in `scripts/`. Agent workflows live in `.cursor/skills/`.

## Thumbnails

- Every mod has `thumbnail_idea.md` (concept + image-generation prompt) and `thumbnail.png` (144×144).
- Thumbnails always use the shared ATMOS frame `assets/thumbnail_frame.png`; never ship raw art without it.
- Workflow: write/update the prompt in `thumbnail_idea.md` → generate square art (no text, no frame) → `py -3 scripts/make_thumbnail.py <art> <mod_folder>`.
- New mods get `thumbnail_idea.md` and a framed thumbnail as part of the scaffold. `thumbnail_idea.md` is excluded from release zips.

## When editing mods

- Follow the `factorio-2.1-modding` skill for prototypes, data lifecycle, and 2.1 API changes.
- Follow the `factorio-mod-packaging` skill when building portal zip releases.
